n","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2025-05-06T19:36:21Z","updated_at":"2025-06-05T11:03:07Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Godot v4.5.dev\n- probably from #85178\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11 (build 26100) - Single-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2070 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7602) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-10750H CPU @ 2.60GHz (12 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nRunning only the `[Editor]` tests creates a `.gdignore` file in the current directory, but running tests should not do this.\n`--test --tc=\"*[Editor]*\"`\n\nThe file is created in `EditorPaths::create();`, which expects the ProjectSettings to already be setup, but it is not setup yet when running those tests alone.\nThis doesn't happen when running all tests because other tests setup ProjectSettings before these ones.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Run the `[Editor]` tests without other tests. E.g. `--test --tc=\"*[Editor]*\"`.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106132/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106132/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}